@@ -97,7 +99,7 @@ Browser source files remain under `js/` to preserve the no-build shell's stable
 | **Collections library reader** | `scripts/book-library-index.mjs` builds the seven-collection catalog from its README indexes and requires every Markdown file under `docs/harshal-systems/` to be accounted for. All 42 files are staged under `book-library/harshal-systems/`, with a generated manifest at `book-library/manifest.json`; `serve.js` exposes only that subtree. The fourth **The Book → Collections (N)** tab reads each file safely and provides its direct GitHub source link |
 | **Manuscript reading view** | `manuscript/` (plaintext chapters and `_collection.json`), `scripts/manuscript-index.mjs` (shared index builder), `js/manuscript.js`, `css/manuscript.css`; rendered inside **The Book → Novel (2) · The Grand River Foundation**. The reader is data-only: chapters are escaped before display, the manifest is generated on request by `serve.js` and at deploy time by `scripts/prepare-assets.mjs`, and only files the index names are published |
 | **Ground-0 engine and workspace** | `js/g0-engine.js`, `js/g0-app.js`, `specs/` |
-| **Research** | `js/g0-research.js`, `research/reports/`, `case-studies/` |
+| **Research** | `js/g0-research.js`, `research/reports/`, `case-studies/`; the NAB insurance framework at `research/neural-atomic-bodies-insurance-requirements.md`, written as a self-contained world model (the Periodic Table of Neural Elements, the OCM 360° Legend read from the print source and checked against `js/ocm-data.js` and `js/ocm-directory.js` through `scripts/nab-world-model.mjs`, and the World Magnetic Model 2025; tested by `tests/nab-world-model-test.mjs`; Accountability-Gated Systems as its law of action, with AI-assisted workflows run as gated discs and protection without permission for sentient life in emergencies, in `scripts/nab-ags.mjs`, checked against `specs/normative/canonical.json` and `js/kernel.js` and tested by `tests/nab-ags-test.mjs`), whose counts are regenerated by `node scripts/nab-insurance-evidence.mjs` from the Compendium rows (`js/nab-sectors.js`), the Ground-0 engine, the register, `research/data/elemental-properties.json`, `research/data/wmm2025.json` (the World Magnetic Model 2025, checked against NCEI's published test values on every run), and `research/data/compound-bodies.json` (27 real substances with measured phase data, read through the compound-body model `scripts/nab-compounds.mjs`, tested by `tests/nab-compounds-test.mjs`, and rebuilt from pinned Python packages by `scripts/build-compound-bodies.py`). It prices nothing and changes no register record |
 | **LLM Link (removed shell)** | `js/apps-llm.js` only. Every model feature was removed — the connection layer, the Ground-0 reading pass, the same-origin Worker relay, the AI binding and its spend ledger, and the suites and guides that served them. The tile keeps its id and opens one `REFUSED — REMOVED` panel that names what used to be here, plus a single deep link into the manual Ground-0 audit wizard: no provider list, key field, model call, or network path exists. See [`docs/REMOVED-LLM-LAYER.md`](REMOVED-LLM-LAYER.md); `npm run test:llm-removal` fails if any of it returns |
 | **Good Intelligence bridge** | `worker/good-intelligence-demo.mjs`, `worker/good-intelligence-tickerbot.mjs`, `js/good-intelligence-assurance.js`, `js/good-intelligence-client.js`, `js/good-intelligence-verifier.js`, `js/good-intelligence-market-context.js`, `js/apps-good-intelligence.js`, `css/good-intelligence.css`, `docs/GOOD-INTELLIGENCE-ASSURANCE.md`; same-origin GET-only demo API with demo-only signed authorization, eight clearly synthetic ticker histories, separate source/claim assurance, and a Market Charts tab for price/Fibonacci, VFI, and WaveTrend line visualizations. No OHLCV means no fabricated chart. It does not implement GI sign-in, publishing, token approvals, or contract transactions. The three user-supplied market Pine v6 scripts related to these calculations and a separate third-party Moon script with unknown author/license are archived in [`scripts/pine/`](../scripts/pine/README.md); parity with the market JS port is unverified |
 | **Characters provider-split market beat (display-only)** | `js/characters-disc-catalog.js`, `js/characters-beat.js`, `js/characters-cast.js`, `js/apps-characters.js`, `worker/characters-beat.mjs`, `worker/characters-massive.mjs`, `worker/characters-crypto-ranking.mjs`, `worker/characters-kraken.mjs`, `worker/characters-futures-contracts.mjs`, and migrations `0005`–`0012`. Tickerbot is Stocks (`1h`/`1d` Characters, `1d` NAB); Kraken Spot is Crypto `1d` (rolling-24-hour USD-pair rank and exact-pair daily bars); Massive is FX/Commodities/Indices `1d` (current active futures contracts, no stale roll). The channels are provider-validated and fail closed with no substitution or fabricated fields. Alpha Vantage/`1mo` is read-only archive history, not a new read/save route. Orb 2 alone has a separate internal Tickerbot `15m` stock warm/intraday lane. Tests: `npm run test:characters` and `npm run test:nab`; design: [`docs/architecture/CHARACTERS-MARKET-BEAT.md`](architecture/CHARACTERS-MARKET-BEAT.md) |
